                                                "sense_id": "946579b4-f885-3817-bb7c-98c5790d45bf",
                                                "text": "Below the hole the mice made in the woodwork was a pile of mealy sawdust."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00856849-7d8c-37cd-9264-613e6cb16a0f",
                                        "entry_id": "54e97666-102d-348a-9aa7-f8afbe144830",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the pale yellow color of a canary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c9a57d9-24f0-47cd-b126-e2983d4ed517",
                                                "sense_id": "00856849-7d8c-37cd-9264-613e6cb16a0f",
                                                "text": "That it is a cross-breed there can be no doubt, from the fact that after a year or two the brilliant colours, both orange and black, begin to fade—the orange fading into a mealy tint, and the black to a dingy grey."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
